---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About The Wog"
	description="Who or what is 'The Wog'?"
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2024')}
	heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Wog in this case is short for Polliwog, and is a nickname of mine, due to my first name being Paul. 
		I was not aware until very recently that it's also a derogatory and racially offensive slur, in some parts of the world.
		Since I'm only using it to describe myself, I hope there is no harm. It's definitely not intended to make anyone feel uncomfortable.
		
		Maybe I should change it to "Blog of the Polliwog". If anyone is even reading this, please let me know if you find that name offensive and I'll change it.
		You could open an issue on [github](https://github.com/pabrams/blogofthewog) about it.
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm a software developer by trade, with a couple of decades of experience in web development, devops, and automated testing, 
		and recently a lot of cloud computing and cloud app development, when I'm at work. I'm also an expert at administering, customizing, using and otherwise 
		manipulating Azure DevOps Services into doing my bidding. At my organization of several thousand developers, testers, business analysts and other supporting staff, we 
		use Azure DevOps Services to track and report on everyone's work. Every team has someone who is handy with that tool, but I'm the person they go to 
		when nobody else knows how to do it.
		I have a post-secondary education in Computer Science, having earned a Bachelor's degree from Carleton University, in Ottawa, Canada.
		I have a lot of interests, so this blog might cover many topics. For the time being, it's where I'm putting descriptions of these little web (or potentially other) 
		apps I've been working on as pet projects. 
	</p>
</Layout>
